{"term":"concert","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:4a5f9517a8e1a9ef21","definition":"To plan together; to settle or adjust by conference, agreement, or consultation.","example":"It was concerted to begin the siege in March.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/concert#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:dc6fd45dd4575127d6","definition":"To plan; to devise; to arrange.","example":"The month ends with a fine day; and I have been walking, and visiting Lewis, and concerting where to see Mr. Harley. I have no news to send you.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/concert#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0cbc882cee35312433","definition":"To act in harmony or conjunction; to form combined plans.","example":"The ministers of Denmark were appointed to concert the matter with Talbot.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/concert#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:152fbb01dec6f9e078","definition":"An agreement in a design or plan; a union formed by mutual communication of opinions and views; an accordance in a scheme; harmony; a simultaneous action.","example":"The dissimilarity in the ingredients which will compose the National Government, and in still more in the manner in which they will be brought into action in its various branches, must form a powerful obstacle to a concert of views, in any partial scheme of elections